/var/home/charlie/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_mrw8lc7unh9ypw_20260723_010057_695955.json:869:          "content": "我已经先把**方案骨架和脚本模板**给你落到电脑上了，可直接在这基础上继续做。\n\n## 已创建的文件\n- 方案说明：\n  - [phone-sync-plan.md](/var/home/charlie/phone-sync-plan.md)\n- 手机端启动脚本模板：\n  - [10-phone-init.sh](/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/10-phone-init.sh)\n- 手机端快照采集脚本模板：\n  - [phone-sync-snapshot.sh](/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/phone-sync-snapshot.sh)\n- 电脑端导入 SQLite 脚本：\n  - [import_phone_snapshots.py](/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/import_phone_snapshots.py)\n- SQLite 数据库已初始化：\n  - [phone_state.db](/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/db/phone_state.db)\n\n## 这套东西现在能做什么\n- 作为你的**永久化手机同步方案骨架**\n- 手机端未来定时输出 `latest.json / state-*.json`\n- 电脑端把这些 JSON 导入：\n  - `snapshots`\n  - `packages`\n- 后面 AI 就可以优先查这个本地库\n\n## 你现在要做的最短步骤\n### 1）把两个手机端脚本放到手机 Termux\n目标位置建议：\n- `~/.termux/boot/10-phone-init.sh`\n- `~/bin/phone-sync-snapshot.sh`\n\n你可以直接把我生成的这两个文件内容复制过去。\n\n### 2）在手机 Termux 里给执行权限\n```bash\nchmod +x ~/.termux/boot/10-phone-init.sh\nchmod +x ~/bin/phone-sync-snapshot.sh\n```\n\n### 3）确保手机侧已装并放行\n- Termux\n- Termux:Boot\n- NetBird\n- root/Magisk\n- 关闭电池优化\n- 允许后台\n- 允许开机自启\n\n### 4）重启手机后验证\n在 Termux 看：\n```bash\ntail -n 50 ~/phone-sync/logs/init.log\nps -ef | grep sshd\n```\n\n### 5）手工跑一次快照\n```bash\n~/bin/phone-sync-snapshot.sh\n```\n\n成功后应产生：\n- `~/phone-sync/out/latest.json`\n- `~/phone-sync/out/state-时间戳.json`\n\n### 6）把 JSON 传到电脑\n先用最简单方式：\n- 手动拷到  \n  `/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/inbox/`\n\n然后电脑端执行：\n```bash\npython /var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/import_phone_snapshots.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## 关键说明\n我现在给你的是**可落地的第一版骨架**，还没做下面这些增强：\n\n- 自动从手机拉文件到电脑\n- 包版本差异比对\n- 软件更新事件检测\n- 指定健康 app 数据目录同步\n- Hermes 定时任务自动导入\n- AI 查询接口封装\n\n这些我下一步可以继续直接帮你补上。\n\n## 我建议下一步直接做\n按优先级：\n\n1. **补自动拉取链路**\n   - 让电脑定时从手机抓 `latest.json`\n2. **补差异检测**\n   - 识别 app 新装/卸载/更新\n3. **补健康 app 专项同步**\n   - 针对“我我身体”做目录/数据库/导出文件跟踪\n4. **接 Hermes 定时任务**\n   - 让它自动入库，AI 直接可查\n\n如果你要，我下一条我就直接继续给你补：\n\n**“电脑端自动拉取 + 更新差异检测 + Hermes 定时任务”**  \n我可以直接把这三部分也写好。"
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_mrw8lc7unh9ypw_20260723_010057_695955.json:944:                "arguments": "{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nimport json\\nimport sqlite3\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\n\\nDB = Path('/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/db/phone_state.db')\\nEVENTS = Path('/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/events')\\nEVENTS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\nOUT = EVENTS / 'package-changes.jsonl'\\n\\nconn = sqlite3.connect(DB)\\nconn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\\ncur = conn.cursor()\\n\\ncur.execute('SELECT id, captured_at, source_file FROM snapshots ORDER BY captured_at DESC, id DESC LIMIT 2')\\nrows = cur.fetchall()\\nif len(rows) < 2:\\n    print('not enough snapshots')\\n    raise SystemExit(0)\\n\\nnewer, older = rows[0], rows[1]\\n\\ncur.execute('SELECT package_name, apk_path FROM packages WHERE snapshot_id=?', (newer['id'],))\\nnew_pkgs = {r['package_name']: r['apk_path'] for r in cur.fetchall()}\\ncur.execute('SELECT package_name, apk_path FROM packages WHERE snapshot_id=?', (older['id'],))\\nold_pkgs = {r['package_name']: r['apk_path'] for r in cur.fetchall()}\\n\\nadded = sorted(set(new_pkgs) - set(old_pkgs))\\nremoved = sorted(set(old_pkgs) - set(new_pkgs))\\nchanged = sorted(p for p in set(new_pkgs) & set(old_pkgs) if new_pkgs[p] != old_pkgs[p])\\n\\npayload = {\\n    'generated_at': datetime.utcnow().isoformat() + 'Z',\\n    'newer_snapshot': dict(newer),\\n    'older_snapshot': dict(older),\\n    'added': [{'package': p, 'apk': new_pkgs[p]} for p in added],\\n    'removed': [{'package': p, 'apk': old_pkgs[p]} for p in removed],\\n    'changed_apk_path': [{'package': p, 'old_apk': old_pkgs[p], 'new_apk': new_pkgs[p]} for p in changed],\\n}\\n\\nwith OUT.open('a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\\n    f.write(json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\\\n')\\n\\nsummary = {\\n    'added': len(added),\\n    'removed': len(removed),\\n    'changed_apk_path': len(changed),\\n    'events_file': str(OUT),\\n}\\nprint(json.dumps(summary, ensure_ascii=False))\\n\",\"cross_profile\":false,\"path\":\"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/detect_package_changes.py\"}"
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_mrx70gsyruus7k_20260723_183040_533213.json:87:          "content": "{\"success\": true, \"name\": \"hermes-studio-task-automation\", \"description\": \"Automate task classification, triage, and routing in Hermes Studio using Jobs (cron), Kanban boards, and LLM-based prompts. Use when the user wants automatic inbox processing, auto-tagging, auto-assignment, scheduled task triage, or rule-based routing in Hermes Studio.\", \"tags\": [], \"related_skills\": [], \"content\": \"---\\nname: hermes-studio-task-automation\\ndescription: Automate task classification, triage, and routing in Hermes Studio using Jobs (cron), Kanban boards, and LLM-based prompts. Use when the user wants automatic inbox processing, auto-tagging, auto-assignment, scheduled task triage, or rule-based routing in Hermes Studio.\\n---\\n\\n# Hermes Studio Task Automation\\n\\n## Problem\\nHermes Studio does not have a built-in rule engine / filter system for automatically classifying tasks or sessions into folders, boards, or statuses based on explicit content rules. The `events` and `homeSubscriptions` capabilities are `partial` or `missing` in current versions, so real-time event-driven automation is not yet supported.\\n\\n## Solution Pattern\\nUse a scheduled Hermes CLI cron job that runs a Python script to:\\n1. Scan recent sessions directly from `~/.hermes/state.db` **and** `~/.hermes-web-ui/hermes-web-ui.db`\\n2. Apply classification rules (keywords + semantic judgment)\\n3. Create tasks on the appropriate board via `hermes kanban create`\\n\\n**Why not Hermes Studio Web UI Jobs?**\\nIn v0.6.32, Web UI Jobs run the LLM agent without forwarding the user's `Authorization` header to Hermes APIs, so API calls inside the Job prompt fail with `401 Missing Authentication header`. The reliable path is `hermes cron` + local script, which reuses the same auth context as `hermes kanban`.\\n\\n## When to Use\\n- User says \\\"自动分类\\\", \\\"自动分拣\\\", \\\"自动归入文件夹\\\", \\\"待办自动识别\\\"\\n- User wants sessions or tasks auto-routed by topic, priority, or status\\n- User wants a periodic inbox triage without manual sorting\\n- User wants recurring maintenance in Hermes Studio, such as auto-updating Hermes or Hermes Studio on a schedule and grouping those jobs under a logical bucket like \\\"软件更新\\\"\\n\\n## Key APIs / Commands\\n- `GET /api/hermes/kanban/boards` — list boards\\n- `POST /api/hermes/kanban/boards` — create board (name, slug, description, icon)\\n- `hermes sessions list --limit N` — list recent sessions (CLI alternative to API)\\n- `POST /api/hermes/kanban?board=<slug>` — create task on a board (JSON body: `title`, `body`, `priority`)\\n- `HERMES_KANBAN_BOARD=<slug> hermes kanban create [--priority N] [--body \\\"...\\\"] [--idempotency-key KEY] [--json] title` — CLI task creation\\n- `GET /api/hermes/kanban/capabilities` — confirm supported features\\n- `hermes cron create --name \\\"...\\\" --script auto_triage.py --no-agent \\\"schedule\\\"` — create scheduled automation\\n- `DELETE /api/hermes/jobs/{id}` / `hermes cron remove <id>` — delete job\\n\\n## Workflow\\n1. **Create category boards**: Create one board per target category, plus an `inbox` board for uncategorized items via `POST /api/hermes/kanban/boards` or `hermes kanban boards create`.\\n2. **Verify task creation**: Create a test task via CLI to confirm access:\\n   ```bash\\n   HERMES_KANBAN_BOARD=<slug> hermes kanban create --priority 2 --json \\\"测试标题\\\" \\\"测试内容\\\"\\n   ```\\n3. **Write classification script**: Use `scripts/auto_triage.py` as the canonical template. The script reads **both** `~/.hermes/state.db` (CLI) and `~/.hermes-web-ui/hermes-web-ui.db` (Web UI), extracts user messages, classifies by keyword rules, and calls `hermes kanban create` with `HERMES_KANBAN_BOARD=<slug>` and `--idempotency-key <session_id>` to prevent duplicates. Important implementation notes: (a) build the classify text as a flat list of strings before joining, because mixing a list return value with string concatenation raises `TypeError`; (b) preload all existing `idempotency_key` values from every `~/.hermes/kanban/boards/*/kanban.db` **excluding archived tasks** befor\n... [truncated]\n...s.\\n4. Write a Markdown report to `/var/home/charlie/.hermes/cron/output/weekly-hermes-review-<date>.md`.\\n5. Surface only material regressions or new reusable patterns; stay silent when nothing changed.\\n\\n## Support Files\\n\\n- `templates/auto-triage-prompt.md` — ready-to-use LLM prompt for session-to-kanban triage\\n- `templates/weekly-review-prompt.md` — prompt for the weekly Hermes task-quality review cron\\n- `references/api-quirks.md` — OpenAPI doc vs actual endpoint discrepancies discovered during automation setup\\n- `references/automation-lessons.md` — stable pipeline, dedupe, command shapes, and failure modes for keyword-based auto-triage\\n\", \"path\": \"devops/hermes-studio-task-automation/SKILL.md\", \"skill_dir\": \"/var/home/charlie/.hermes/skills/devops/hermes-studio-task-automation\", \"linked_files\": {\"references\": [\"references/api-quirks.md\", \"references/automation-lessons.md\", \"references/hs-cli-pattern.md\"], \"templates\": [\"templates/auto-triage-prompt.md\", \"templates/weekly-review-prompt.md\", \"templates/update-hermes.sh\"], \"scripts\": [\"scripts/auto_triage.py\"]}, \"usage_hint\": \"To view linked files, call skill_view(name, file_path) where file_path is e.g. 'references/api.md' or 'assets/config.yaml'\", \"required_environment_variables\": [], \"required_commands\": [], \"missing_required_environment_variables\": [], \"missing_credential_files\": [], \"missing_required_commands\": [], \"setup_needed\": false, \"setup_skipped\": false, \"readiness_status\": \"available\"}",
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_mrx7k13qrulyf4_20260723_183149_144548.json:199:          "content": "{\"total_count\": 23, \"files\": [\"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/logs/run-sync.log\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/logs/pull.log\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/ssh-command-queue-plan.md\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/sample-phone-command.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/get-phone-command-result.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/send-phone-command.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/phone-command-listener.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/termux-root-triage.md\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/logs/setup-phone.log\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/import_phone_snapshots.py\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/detect_package_changes.py\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/pull_phone_latest.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/phone-sync-snapshot.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/setup-phone-sync.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/install-termux-boot-template.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/phone-keepalive.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/10-phone-remote-magisk.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/root-remote-control-plan.md\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/__pycache__/detect_package_changes.cpython-314.pyc\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/__pycache__/import_phone_snapshots.cpython-314.pyc\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/run_phone_sync.sh\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/db/phone_state.db\", \"/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/scripts/10-phone-init.sh\"]}",
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_mrx7k13qrulyf4_20260723_183149_144548.json:272:                "arguments": "{\"background\":false,\"command\":\"python - <<'PY'\\nimport sqlite3, json\\nfor db in ['/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/db/phone_state.db','/var/home/charlie/phone-sync/phone-sync.db']:\\n    try:\\n        conn=sqlite3.connect(db)\\n        cur=conn.cursor()\\n        cur.execute(\\\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table'\\\")\\n        tables=[r[0] for r in cur.fetchall()]\\n        print('DB', db)\\n        print('TABLES', tables)\\n        for t in tables:\\n            try:\\n                cur.execute(f'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM {t}')\\n                print(t, cur.fetchone()[0])\\n            except Exception as e:\\n                print(t, 'ERR', e)\\n        conn.close()\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        print('DB', db, 'ERR', e)\\nPY\",\"notify_on_complete\":false,\"pty\":false,\"timeout\":120,\"watch_patterns\":[],\"workdir\":\"/var/home/charlie\"}"
