文本**发来，我就直接给你第一版迁移方案。"
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_20260726_021247_16b30b_20260726_021559_714520.json:285:          "content": "{\"success\": true, \"name\": \"hermes-runtime-debugging\", \"description\": \"Diagnose and resolve Hermes Agent / Hermes Studio runtime errors such as unknown run, bridge failures, session loss, in-memory state issues, and tasks that stop unexpectedly due to systemd-level restarts of sibling AI agent services. Use when the user pastes a Hermes traceback, reports 'unknown run', asks why a Hermes Studio task/run disappeared or failed, reports tasks stopping by themselves, or reports that refreshing the Web UI or switching tasks causes in-progress work to restart. User preference: Hermes must never be suspended or auto-stopped by auxiliary managers; preserve Hermes services in smart-service-manager, idle-sleep, and systemd suspend hooks. Default to a tiered service lifecycle: always_on for core infrastructure, on_demand_persistent for user-started AI services, transient for lightweight helpers.\", \"tags\": [\"hermes\", \"runtime\", \"debugging\", \"bridge\", \"troubleshooting\"], \"related_skills\": [], \"content\": \"---\\nname: hermes-runtime-debugging\\ndescription: \\\"Diagnose and resolve Hermes Agent / Hermes Studio runtime errors such as unknown run, bridge failures, session loss, in-memory state issues, and tasks that stop unexpectedly due to systemd-level restarts of sibling AI agent services. Use when the user pastes a Hermes traceback, reports 'unknown run', asks why a Hermes Studio task/run disappeared or failed, reports tasks stopping by themselves, or reports that refreshing the Web UI or switching tasks causes in-progress work to restart. User preference: Hermes must never be suspended or auto-stopped by auxiliary managers; preserve Hermes services in smart-service-manager, idle-sleep, and systemd suspend hooks. Default to a tiered service lifecycle: always_on for core infrastructure, on_demand_persistent for user-started AI services, transient for lightweight helpers.\\\"\\nversion: 1.2.0\\nauthor: Ekko\\nlicense: MIT\\nplatforms: [linux]\\nmetadata:\\n  hermes:\\n    tags: [hermes, runtime, debugging, bridge, troubleshooting]\\nprerequisites:\\n  commands: [grep, find, journalctl]\\n  tools: [mcp_hermes_studio_api_hermes_studio_api_request, terminal]\\n---\\n\\n# Hermes Runtime Debugging\\n\\nDiagnose runtime-level Hermes Agent / Hermes Studio failures where the root cause is in-process state, bridge lifecycle, or service uptime, not user config values.\\n\\n## When to use\\n\\n- User reports `unknown run: <uuid>` or similar bridge/runtime errors.\\n- A Hermes Studio run disappears after a refresh or restart.\\n- User asks why a completed/in-progress Hermes task is no longer accessible.\\n- User reports that refreshing the Web UI or switching tasks causes in-progress work to stop or restart from scratch.\\n- Need to distinguish config issues from runtime/memory-lifecycle issues.\\n- User reports tasks stopping \\\"by themselves\\\" with no manual intervention.\\n- Need to determine whether a systemd-level restart/kill affects both a sibling AI backend and Hermes.\\n\\n## Quick diagnosis flow\\n\\n### 0. Distinguish execution slowdown from UI refresh lag\\n\\nWhen a user says Hermes feels slow unless they open the conversation, do not assume the run only starts on page focus. Check three layers separately:\\n\\n- **Worker/runtime reality**: inspect Hermes Studio worker/runtime status first. If bridge is reachable, workers are `running=true`, and `runningSessionCount` / `interacting_session_count` are non-zero, the backend is still executing even if the UI looks stale.\\n- **Provider/model health**: inspect recent `errors` log entries and usage concentration. If the high-volume model/provider shows repeated `APIConnectionError`, `APITimeoutError`, `Connection error`, or `Request timed out`, treat upstream latency/retries as the primary cause of slowness.\\n- **Front-end visibility effects**: if the page appears to wake up when opened, treat it as a status-sync/output-subscription suspicion unless proven otherwise. Look for WebSocket usage, `visibilitychange`, and server-side `background_poll` / `get_output` paths before claiming hidden tabs pause execution.\\n\\nFor this class of report, conclude carefully:\\n- \\\"后台没跑\\\" requires direct evidence that workers/sessions are idle or unreachable.\\n- If workers are active but the user only sees progress after opening the chat, describe it as **\\\"后台在跑，但前台页面的实时反馈更明显\\\"** unless you find code proving hidden-page execution is gated.\\n\\n### 0.55 Mobile browser refresh / foreground-background transitions cause disconnect\\n\\nIf the user reports that **phone browser refresh, switching apps, or returning to the Hermes Web UI causes in-progress work to appear broken, delayed, or restarted**, treat this as a **frontend-backend disconnect/reconnect** symptom:\\n\\n- **Mobile browsers aggressively kill WebSocket/JS** when a page is refreshed, backgrounded, or restored. The Socket.IO client in Hermes Web UI (`chat-COpttEcl.js`) does support `reconnection: true` and emits `resume` on reconnect, but the UI may still show blank/stale state until `resumed` or `run.reattach_failed` arrives.\\n- **Backend session/run usually survives** because `bridge_pool.py` keeps `AgentSession` and `RunRecord` in memory. A frontend refresh does **not** destroy the server-side run by itself.\\n- **What the user experiences as \\\"断/重新执行\\\"** is typically:\\n  1. WebSocket drops → streaming output stops.\\n  2. Frontend reloads page state from local caches / session metadata.\\n  3. Socket reconnects → `resumeSession` → `reattachBridgeRun` attempts to reattach to the existing run.\\n  4. If reattach succeeds, the UI catches up; if it fails or times out, the run looks dead and the user may manually reissue the request.\\n\\n**Diagnosis:**\\n1. Check for `run.reattach_failed` events in Hermes Web UI server logs or frontend console.\\n2. Confirm the session still exists in `state.db` and `ended_at IS NULL`.\\n3. Confirm the bridge worker is still alive and `session.running` is true.\\n4. Check `request_dump_*.json` for fresh failures; if the run is still alive but the user sees delays, it is likely reconnect/UI sync lag rather than true backend restart.\\n\\n**Mitigation for the user:**\\n- After phone refresh, wait a few seconds for `resumed` / reattach before reissuing input.\\n- On mobile, prefer adding the Web UI to the home screen / using a PWA-like shortcut to reduce browser lifecycle kills.\\n- Avoid manual refresh while a long Hermes run is active unless the UI is completely unresponsive.\\n- If the user has multiple profiles, switching to another profile while one is reconnecting preserves productivity; profile isolation limits blast radius.\\n\\n### 0.52 Web UI session list number is not a valid resume target\\n\\nIf the user tries to resume from the Hermes Web UI session list by typing `/resume <number>` or similar, and it appears to do nothing, treat this as a **CLI/UI semantics mismatch**, not a runtime failure:\\n\\n- **Symptom:** User sees numbered sessions in the Web UI sidebar/list, types `/resume 1` in the chat input, and expects Session #1 to resume.\\n- **Root cause:** The displayed numbers are **UI list indices only**. They are not session IDs, and Hermes chat does **not** implement `/resume` as a slash command. The input is treated as a normal message or ignored.\\n- **Correct resume paths:**\\n  1. **Web UI:** click the target session directly in the sidebar/list.\\n  2. **CLI:** `hermes chat --resume <session_id>` (use the actual ID shown in `hermes sessions list`, e.g. `20260725_004149_2f38e6`).\\n  3. **CLI:** `hermes -c` to resume the most recent session, or `hermes -c \\\"session name\\\"` for name-based resume.\\n  4. **CLI interactive:** `hermes sessions browse` to pick a session visually.\\n- **Diagnosis:** If unsure whether a session exists or is active, run `hermes sessions list` to see real IDs and timestamps. Do not confuse the `ID` column with the row number.\\n\\n### 0.5 Refresh/switch causes in-progress work to restart\\n\\nIf the user reports that **refreshing the Hermes Web UI or switching to another task causes the current work to stop and restart from scratch**, treat this as a likely **runtime/bridge state loss** symptom rather than a frontend-only bug:\\n\\n- **Primary cause:** the Web UI / agent-bridge process was previously interrupted by an auxiliary manager (`smart-service-manager`, `idle-sleep`, systemd suspend hooks). The bridge stores active runs in memory; after interruption, the in-memory state is gone.\\n- **Secondary cause:** the Web UI or bridge process restarted for unrelated reasons, clearing in-memory `RunRecord` entries.\\n- **Diagnosis:**\\n  1. Check `journalctl --user -u hermes-web-ui` for recent stop/start/SIGTERM lines.\\n  2. Check `journalctl --user -u smart-service-manager` and `journalctl --user -u idle-sleep.service` for stop events.\\n  3. Correlate timestamps: the refresh/switch complaint usually appears shortly after a service interruption.\\n- **Workaround:** do not refresh or switch tasks during long-running Hermes work until the anti-idle preservation fix is confirmed.\\n- **Fix:** apply the full anti-idle playbook in `references/hermes-anti-idle-preserve.md`, then verify with a long task + page refresh.\\n\\n### 0.6 Switching tasks feels like re-execution or delayed response\\n\\nIf the user reports that **switching Hermes tasks/chats causes visible delay, blank periods, or feels like the task is running again**, do not assume the session was destroyed. Check the execution topology first:\\n\\n- **Multi-session, potentially single-worker:** Hermes supports many concurrent sessions in `state.db`, but the default profile often runs only **one** `hermes_bridge.py --worker-profile default` process. That means agent turns are **serial** across all default-profile sessions. A long task in Session A blocks Session B until the worker is free.\\n- **Session isolation:** each Hermes session has its own message history. Switching to another session naturally shows a different context, which can feel like a \\\"fresh start\\\" even when the prior session is still active.\\n- **Upstream quota/cooldown masking:** repeated `403 insufficient_user_quota` or `429 model_cooldown` failures in `request_dump_*.json` produce retry loops. The UI may show repeated \\\"running\\\" indicators or partial restarts that feel like re-execution.\\n\\n**Diagnosis:**\\n1. Confirm active sessions:\\n   ```bash\\n   python3 - <<'PY'\\n   import sqlite3\\n   con = sqlite3.connect('/var/home/charlie/.hermes/state.db')\\n   for row in con.execute(\\\"SELECT id, model, started_at, ended_at, message_count FROM sessions WHERE ended_at IS NULL ORDER BY started_at DESC LIMIT 20;\\\"):\\n       print(row)\\n   con.close()\\n   PY\\n   ```\\n2. Check worker count:\\n   ```bash\\n   ps aux | grep 'hermes_bridge.py --worker-profile default' | grep -v grep\\n   ```\\n   If only **1** line appears, default-profile work is serial.\\n3. Inspect recent request dumps for quota/cooldown errors:\\n   ```bash\\n   python3 - <<'PY'\\n   import json, glob, os\\n   for f in sorted(glob.glob('/var/home/charlie/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_*.json'), key=os.path.getmtime)[-5:]:\\n       with open(f) as fh: d=json.load(fh)\\n       print(d.get('timestamp'), d.get('session_id'), d.get('reason'), (d.get('error') or {}).get('message','')[:140])\\n   PY\\n   ```\\n4. Check provider health/quota in the upstream console rather than retrying blindly.\\n\\n**Fixes:**\\n- Upstream quota issue: recharge or switch to a fallback provider/model; do not retry the same failing credential.\\n- Serial worker bottleneck: if the installed Hermes Web UI supports multiple worker profiles or parallel workers, add/adjust them so sessions can execute in parallel.\\n- UX clarity: stay in the same session for continuations; treat session switches as context switches, not continuation of the prior thread.\\n- **Profile-based parallelism:** when `config.yaml` contains `multiplex_profiles: true`, create separate Hermes profiles and start additional bridge workers with `--worker-profile <profile>`. Each profile gets its own worker process, allowing true parallel execution across profiles. See `references/multiplex-worker-profile-setup.md` for the exact commands and verification steps.\\n- **Worker idle behavior:** profile workers may exit when idle and are lazily restarted on the next request. This is normal; do not treat an absent idle worker as a failure.\\n- **Coding Plan quota awareness:** if the provider uses a Coding Plan endpoint (e.g. `https://api.stepfun.com/step_plan/v1`), quota errors may appear as `insufficient_user_quota` with rapidly decreasing `用户剩余额度` even when the regular API channel seems fine. Recharge or switch providers; do not rely on fallback credentials that route to the same exhausted Coding Plan pool. See `references/stepfun-coding-plan-quirks.md`.\\n- **Non-default profile env pitfall:** when adding profiles `p1`..`pN`, you must copy `~/.hermes/.env` into each profile directory. Non-default profiles load env via `_apply_profile_dotenv`, which clears shared env keys first and loads only the profile's `.env`. Missing `.env` causes auth failures that look like provider errors.\\n\\n### 1. Classify the error source\\n\\n| Layer | Typical signal | Where to look |\\n|------|----------------|---------------|\\n| Hermes Web UI bridge | `unknown run: ...` from `bridge_broker.py` / `bridge_pool.py` | `hermes-web-ui/dist/server/agent-bridge/python/bridge_pool.py` |\\n| Hermes CLI / gateway | reconnect failures, platform refused, drain warnings | `~/.hermes/logs/gateway.log`, `errors.log` |\\n| Coding agent run | missing `sessionId`, native launch failures | Hermes Studio `/api/coding-agents` + coding agent logs |\\n\\n### 2. Probe the Hermes Studio API first\\n\\nBefore reading server source, check whether the run/session is visible to the running instance:\\n\\n- `GET /api/coding-agents` — is the coding agent installed and healthy?\\n- `hermes_studio_use_sessions_list` — does the session still exist?\\n- `hermes_studio_use_workflows_list` — was this a workflow run?\\n\\nIf the ID is absent from all three, it is likely an in-memory bridge run that has already been cleaned up.\\n\\n### 3. Trace the exact message to the runtime bundle\\n\\nFor Hermes Web UI errors, search the installed server bundle:\\n\\n```bash\\ngrep -rn \\\"unknown run\\\" /var/home/charlie/.nvm/versions/node/v*/lib/node_modules/hermes-web-ui/dist/server/agent-bridge/python/\\n```\\n\\nThis identifies the exact method raising the error (`RunRecord.get_result`, `RunRecord.get_output`, etc.) and confirms whether the failure is a missing in-memory record vs a database lookup failure.\\n\\n### 4. Check service uptime and restarts\\n\\n```bash\\nps aux | grep -i hermes | grep -v grep\\njournalctl --user -u hermes-web-ui --since \\\"30 minutes ago\\\" --no-pager\\n```\\n\\nA recent Hermes Web UI restart almost always explains missing run IDs: `RunRecord` entries live only in the Python bridge process memory.\\n\\n**Also check for stale systemd stop timing.** If gateway/web-ui logs warn that `TimeoutStopSec` is lower than `drain_timeout`, treat that as a runtime-risk amplifier even when it is not the immediate cause of the user's symptom. Fix by installing or adding a user-systemd override so `TimeoutStopSec >= drain_timeout + buffer` (for example 240s for a 180s drain timeout), then `systemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user restart hermes-web-ui` and verify with `systemctl --user show hermes-web-ui.service -p TimeoutStopUSec`.\\n\\n### 5. Check for browser-facing illusion vs real backend slowness\\n\\nWhen the user reports \\\"it only runs after I open the conversation\\\", verify both layers:\\n\\n- **Backend actually running**: inspect worker/runtime status and logs; a running worker with updating `lastUsedAt` / `runningSessionCount` means the task is not blocked purely by UI focus.\\n- **Frontend visibility effects**: the UI may refresh or subscribe more aggressively when a conversation tab is open, so output can appear to \\\"start\\\" only after focus changes.\\n- **API retry symptoms**: repeated `APIConnectionError`, `APITimeoutError`, `Connection error`, or `Request timed out` in `errors.log` usually explain the perceived stall better than a frontend bug.\\n- **Do not conclude focus-triggered execution without evidence**. Prefer: \\\"后台在跑，但前台刷新更明显/上游慢\\\" unless logs show a hard pause.\\n\\n### 6. Check service-stop timeout mismatches\\n\\nIf `gateway.log` warns about a stale `TimeoutStopSec` / `drain_timeout` mismatch, fix the user service drop-in so systemd does not interrupt a clean drain on restart. Verify the active unit with `systemctl --user show hermes-web-ui.service -p TimeoutStopUSec -p ActiveState -p SubState` after reloading.\\n\\nWhen Hermes tasks stop unexpectedly with no clear app-level error, check whether Hermes runs inside a sibling AI agent's systemd cgroup. If so, that service's watchdog or lifecycle scripts may be killing Hermes as collateral.\\n\\n**Investigation triad:**\\n\\n1. **journalctl** — look for systemd stop/start cycles of the parent service and SIGKILL lines mentioning `hermes`\\n2. **systemd timers** — identify watchdog/cleaner timers (`list-timers`, unit files)\\n3. **cgroup relationship** — confirm Hermes PID appears in the sibling service's stop/kill journal entries\\n\\n**Upstream sanity check:** before concluding the backend has a bug, search the upstream repo (e.g. `repo:opencode-ai/opencode abort OR watchdog OR \\\"session stop\\\"`). If no upstream issue exists, the failure is almost certainly environmental.\\n\\n**Common patterns:**\\n- `opencode-health-watchdog.sh` restarts `opencode.service` on `tasks_>N`, `api_http_000`, `api_slow`, memory pressure, `duplicate_mcp`\\n- `opencode-stuck-cleaner.sh` aborts `busy` sessions without active CLI clients\\n- `KillMode=mixed` + `TimeoutStopSec=30` means SIGTERM first, then SIGKILL — all cgroup children die\\n\\nSee `references/sibling-agent-cgroup-casualties.md` for the full investigation pattern and evidence template.\\n\\n## Known root causes and fixes\\n\\n### Provider retry exhaustion (`max_retries_exhausted`)\\n- **Symptoms:** A run stops with no obvious local traceback; the session remains in `working: true` or jumps to `working: false` without a clean end state.\\n- **Investigation:**\\n  1. Check `~/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_*.json` for the session ID.\\n  2. Look for `\\\"reason\\\": \\\"max_retries_exhausted\\\"` in the dumped request.\\n  3. Note the upstream provider/model and whether the same dump shows repeated retry-style calls.\\n- **Fix:** Treat it as an upstream/provider reliability issue first. Tune `fallback_providers` / `fallback_model` in `~/.hermes/config.yaml`, or rerun during a clearer network window.\\n- **Prevention:** Do not assume every Hermes stop is a Web UI or bridge bug; provider-side exhaustion is a first-class termination path.\\n\\n### Provider quota exhaustion (`insufficient_user_quota`)\\n- **Symptoms:** Runs stall or fail with `403 insufficient_user_quota`; `request_dump_*.json` shows rapidly decreasing `用户剩余额度` balances; retries make the delay worse without progressing.\\n- **Investigation:**\\n  1. Search `request_dump_*.json` for the affected `session_id`.\\n  2. Confirm the error code is `insufficient_user_quota` and note the requested vs remaining amount.\\n  3. Verify whether fallback providers are configured and whether they are also exhausted.\\n  4. **Distinguish Coding Plan from custom providers:** inspect the `provider` and `base_url` fields in the dump. A `provider` of `aieyra` (or any custom provider) means the 403 is from that provider, not StepFun Coding Plan. See `references/stepfun-coding-plan-quirks.md`.\\n- **Fix:** Recharge or switch providers/models. Do not keep retrying the same exhausted credential.\\n- **Prevention:** Treat quota alerts as first-class Hermes runtime failures, not network blips.\\n\\n### Missing session end-state in `state.db`\\n- **Symptoms:** Completed runs still look \\\"in progress\\\" in Hermes Studio (`ended_at` and `end_reason` are NULL) even though the model returned a final answer.\\n- **Investigation:**\\n  1. Query the local DB:\\n     ```bash\\n     python3 - <<'PY'\\n     import sqlite3\\n     con = sqlite3.connect('/var/home/charlie/.hermes/state.db')\\n     cur = con.cursor()\\n     print('tables:', [r[0] for r in cur.execute(\\\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' ORDER BY name;\\\")])\\n     cur.execute(\\\"PRAGMA table_info(sessions);\\\")\\n     print('sessions cols:', [c[1] for c in cur.fetchall()])\\n     for row in cur.execute(\\\"SELECT id, model, started_at, ended_at, end_reason, title FROM sessions ORDER BY COALESCE(ended_at, started_at) DESC LIMIT 20;\\\"):\\n         print(row)\\n     con.close()\\n     PY\\n     ```\\n  2. If recent active sessions all show `ended_at=NULL` and `end_reason=NULL`, the stop likely happened without state persistence.\\n- **Upstream context:** This matches upstream Hermes Studio issues around bridge-run termination not writing session lifecycle fields. Search upstream with:\\n  - `repo:EKKOLearnAI/hermes-studio \\\"ended_at\\\" \\\"end_reason\\\"`\\n  - `repo:EKKOLearnAI/hermes-studio \\\"思考中\\\"`\\n  - `repo:EKKOLearnAI/hermes-studio \\\"max_retries_exhausted\\\"`\\n- **Fix:** Restart the affected session manually until the upstream persistence fix lands in the installed version.\\n\\n### `unknown run: <uuid>`\\n- **Cause:** Hermes Web UI Agent Bridge stores active runs in `BridgePool._runs` (in-memory). When the bridge process restarts, or when a completed run is pruned, the ID vanishes.\\n- **Fix:** Refresh the Hermes Studio page and re-run the task.\\n- **Prevention:** For long-running or critical work, use Hermes Studio Sessions or Workflows rather than relying on transient bridge runs.\\n\\n### Coding agent run not found\\n- **Cause:** Session was destroyed, or the run was never persisted.\\n- **Fix:** Start a fresh run via `/api/coding-agents/{id}/runs` with an explicit `sessionId`.\\n\\n### Tasks killed by sibling AI agent service restart\\n- **Cause:** Hermes runs as a child process of another AI agent backend (e.g., `opencode.service`), or that backend's watchdog/cleaner scripts actively abort sessions. Two common mechanisms:\\n  1. **cgroup kill** — parent service restarts, `KillMode=mixed` SIGKILLs all cgroup children.\\n  2. **session abort** — a stuck-cleaner script POSTs `/session/{id}/abort` on `busy` sessions that have no attached CLI client, even if a web/remote client is still connected.\\n- **Fix:** Isolate Hermes from the sibling service's cgroup, tune watchdog thresholds, and make stuck-cleaner client detection aware of non-CLI sessions.\\n- **Prevention:** Always check cgroup relationships when deploying multiple AI agent backends on the same host. Validate script changes with `bash -n` and a dry-run tick before relying on them.\\n\\n### Hermes Web UI local proxy crash loop (`EADDRINUSE`)\\n- **Symptoms:** `hermes-8648-proxy.service` shows rapid restart cycles with `Error: listen EADDRINUSE: address already in use 0.0.0.0:8648` while the backend `:18648` remains healthy.\\n- **Cause:** The front proxy script does not handle `EADDRINUSE` on `server.listen(8648)`.\\n- **Fix:** Add an `error` listener that retries `listen()` after 1s when `e.code === 'EADDRINUSE'`. See `references/hermes-webui-proxy-stability.md` for the exact patch.\\n- **Verification:** After restart, `journalctl --user -u hermes-8648-proxy.service` should show a single `listening on :8648 -> :18648` line and no immediate `EADDRINUSE` stack traces.\\n\\n### FRP duplicate-client proxy conflicts (`already exists` / `port unavailable`)\\n- **Symptoms:** `frpc.service` repeatedly logs `start error: proxy [...] already exists` and occasionally `port unavailable`; public Hermes access flaps even though backend services are up.\\n- **Cause:** Multiple `frpc` processes are running for the same config file, often because a manual/deviation `frpc` instance was left running alongside the systemd `frpc.service`.\\n- **Fix:** Kill non-systemd `frpc` processes, then restart `frpc.service` so proxy registration is clean. See `references/hermes-webui-proxy-stability.md` for the safe cleanup commands.\\n- **Verification:** After cleanup, `ps -eo pid,etime,cmd | grep frpc | grep -v grep` should show only the systemd-managed frpc plus the system `frps`; new `frpc` logs should no longer flood with duplicate-proxy warnings.\\n\\n### OpenCode task stops (watchdog / stuck-cleaner)\\n- **Symptoms:** Hermes sessions end with `end_reason: \\\"error\\\"` around the same time as `opencode.service` restarts, or `stuck-cleaner.log` shows `abort_stale_busy` for active sessions.\\n- **Investigation:**\\n  1. Correlate Hermes session `updated_at` with `journalctl --user -u opencode.service` stop/start lines.\\n  2. Check `~/.local/state/opencode-lifecycle/health-watchdog.log` for `tasks_*`, `api_slow_*`, `defer_restart`.\\n  3. Check `~/.local/state/opencode-lifecycle/stuck-cleaner.log` for `abort_stale_busy` and `abort_completed_assistant_stale_busy`.\\n- **Fix (validated 2026-07-22):**\\n  - `opencode-health-watchdog.sh`: raise `tasks` threshold (e.g. `180→400`) and `api_slow` window (e.g. `5s→15s`).\\n  - `opencode-stuck-cleaner.sh`: remove `completed_assistant_stale_busy` abort branch; extend `STALE_MESSAGE_SECONDS` and `ORPHAN_EMPTY_ASSISTANT_SECONDS`; broaden `active_client_for()` to recognize any `opencode` process whose command line includes the target `session_id`.\\n- **Prevention:** Keep `.bak-<timestamp>` backups before editing lifecycle scripts, and run `bash -n` after each change.\\n\\n### Idle/suspend/soft-stop from auxiliary service managers\\n- **Symptoms:** Hermes runs stop after a predictable idle window (often 10-20 minutes), or right before system suspend, with no app-level error. **Follow-up symptom:** after the user refreshes the Hermes Web UI or switches tasks, in-progress work is lost and restarts from scratch.\\n- **Investigation:**\\n  1. Check whether an auxiliary manager is installed: `systemctl --user status smart-service-manager` (or equivalents).\\n  2. Inspect its config for `soft_stop`, `suspend_stop`, or `protected` lists that mention `hermes-web-ui.service`.\\n  3. Check **independent watchdog scripts** such as `~/.local/bin/idle-sleep.sh`; they may stop services by unit-name pattern without consulting `protected` lists.\\n  4. Check **timer units** for `smart-service-manager-suspend.timer` and `idle-sleep.timer`; disable them if present.\\n  5. Correlate stop timestamps with `journalctl --user -u smart-service-manager` and `journalctl --user -u idle-sleep.service`.\\n- **Fix (validated 2026-07-24):** Apply the tiered service lifecycle pattern in `references/tiered-service-lifecycle.md`. Do not rely on ad-hoc `PROTECTED_SERVICES` hacks.\\n  - Split services into `always_on`, `on_demand_persistent`, and `transient` tiers in `smart-service-manager/config.json`.\\n  - Restrict `suspend_stop`, `soft_stop`, and `hard_stop` to `transient` only.\\n  - Rewrite `idle-sleep.sh` to read `tiers.transient` from `config.json` instead of maintaining a static protected list.\\n  - Patch `do_pre_suspend()` to honor `protected` before enumerating `suspend_stop`.\\n  - Add user-systemd drop-ins for `hermes-web-ui.service` and `hermes-gateway.service` with `Restart=always`, `StopWhenUnneeded=no`, and sufficient `TimeoutStopSec`.\\n  - Disable `smart-service-manager-suspend.timer`; keep `idle-sleep.timer` enabled only because it now targets transient services exclusively.\\n- **Prevention:** When deploying Hermes alongside other AI backends, always audit auxiliary lifecycle managers and independent watchdog scripts for implicit stop/kill policies before treating every stop as a Hermes bug.\\n\\n**Validated anti-idle recipe:** see `references/hermes-anti-idle-preserve.md` for step-by-step commands and `references/tiered-service-lifecycle.md` for the tiered config schema, script patches, and validation steps.\\n\\n### StepFun Coding Plan quota behavior (`insufficient_user_quota`)\\n- **Symptoms:** Runs stall with `403 insufficient_user_quota`; `request_dump_*.json` shows rapidly decreasing `用户剩余额度` balances; the provider channel is `https://api.stepfun.com/step_plan/v1` (Coding Plan) rather than the standard API channel.\\n- **Investigation:**\\n  1. Check `~/.hermes/.env` or config for `STEPFUN_BASE_URL`. If it contains `/step_plan/v1`, the account is on Coding Plan.\\n  2. Search `request_dump_*.json` for the affected `session_id` and confirm `insufficient_user_quota`.\\n  3. Verify fallback providers are configured; if they route to the same Coding Plan pool, they will also be exhausted.\\n  4. **Distinguish from custom provider 403s:** check the `provider` field in the dump. If it says `aieyra` or another custom provider, the quota error is from that provider, not StepFun Coding Plan. See `references/stepfun-coding-plan-quirks.md`.\\n- **Fix:** Recharge the Coding Plan account or switch to a non-Coding-Plan provider/model. Do not keep retrying the same exhausted credential/channel.\\n- **Prevention:** Monitor `request_dump_*.json` for `insufficient_user_quota` and treat Coding Plan quota alerts as first-class runtime failures, not transient network blips.\\n\\n### Web UI shutdown chain (SIGTERM → bridge abort → force exit)\\n- **Mechanism:** On `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT`/`SIGUSR2`, the Web UI closes `ChatRunSocket`, iterates all tracked sessions, and calls `abortController.abort()`. If `HERMES_AGENT_BRIDGE_STOP_ON_SHUTDOWN` is true (default in production), it also calls `agentBridge.stop()`. After a 15s grace window (`lqI=15e3`), it force-stops managed children and calls `process.exit(0)`.\\n- **Implication:** Any systemd restart, or auxiliary manager stop, sends `SIGTERM` and triggers this chain. Runs that look healthy up to the shutdown second are still terminated.\\n- **Mitigation:**\\n  1. Set `HERMES_AGENT_BRIDGE_STOP_ON_SHUTDOWN=0` in the Hermes Web UI environment so sibling-service restarts do not murder the bridge/runtime.\\n  2. Set `HERMES_WEB_UI_SHUTDOWN_FORCE_EXIT_MS=60000` (or higher) to give long-running runs a larger graceful window.\\n  3. Prefer `systemctl --user reload hermes-web-ui` or in-place config changes over full restarts during heavy tasks.\\n\\n### Repair recipe for SIGTERM-induced stops\\nUse this when journalctl confirms `SIGTERM` from an auxiliary manager or systemd restart:\\n\\n1. **Protect the service** — add `hermes-web-ui.service` to `protected` in `smart-service-manager/config.json` and remove it from `soft_stop`/`suspend_stop`.\\n2. **Preserve the bridge** — set `HERMES_AGENT_BRIDGE_STOP_ON_SHUTDOWN=0` in the launch script or unit file.\\n3. **Extend the grace window** — set `HERMES_WEB_UI_SHUTDOWN_FORCE_EXIT_MS=60000`.\\n4. **Backfill killed sessions** — for each SIGTERM window, update `ended_at` and `end_reason='shutdown'` for sessions whose last message falls within the window and that have at least one message. See `references/hermes-sigterm-repair-playbook.md` for the exact SQLite query template.\\n5. **Tune agent retries** — if the user can edit `~/.hermes/config.yaml` manually, recommend `restart_drain_timeout: 300` and `api_max_retries: 5`. If the file is protected/credential-locked, surface this as a manual step instead of auto-patching.\\n6. **Verify** — run the checklist in `references/hermes-sigterm-repair-playbook.md`.\\n\\n### Monitoring / baseline (after fix)\\n- Monitor `journalctl --user -u hermes-web-ui` for repeat SIGTERM entries.\\n- Periodically query `state.db` for `ended_at IS NULL` count; a sudden spike means a new unhandled stop event.\\n- If `request_dump_*.json` starts showing fresh `max_retries_exhausted` entries, investigate provider health before rerunning.\", \"path\": \"devops/hermes-runtime-debugging/SKILL.md\", \"skill_dir\": \"/var/home/charlie/.hermes/skills/devops/hermes-runtime-debugging\", \"linked_files\": {\"references\": [\"references/bridge-pool-run-lifecycle.md\", \"references/sibling-agent-cgroup-casualties.md\", \"references/opencode-recurrence-log.md\", \"references/hermes-session-state-audit.md\", \"references/hermes-sigterm-repair-playbook.md\", \"references/hermes-anti-idle-preserve.md\", \"references/tiered-service-lifecycle.md\", \"references/stepfun-coding-plan-quirks.md\", \"references/multiplex-worker-profile-setup.md\", \"references/frontend-refresh-vs-backend-slowness.md\", \"references/session-resume-gotchas.md\", \"references/hermes-webui-proxy-stability.md\"]}, \"usage_hint\": \"To view linked files, call skill_view(name, file_path) where file_path is e.g. 'references/api.md' or 'assets/config.yaml'\", \"required_environment_variables\": [], \"required_commands\": [], \"missing_required_environment_variables\": [], \"missing_credential_files\": [], \"missing_required_commands\": [], \"setup_needed\": false, \"setup_skipped\": false, \"readiness_status\": \"available\", \"metadata\": {\"hermes\": {\"tags\": [\"hermes\", \"runtime\", \"debugging\", \"bridge\", \"troubleshooting\"]}}}",
/var/home/charlie/.hermes/sessions/request_dump_324f1d8e687a_20260801_005821_877444.json:41:          "content": "{\"success\": true, \"name\": \"ops-autopilot\", \"description\": \"Autonomous ops pilot for Hermes: discover, diagnose, repair, and evolve local/network/phone issues without manual scaffolding. Use when the user wants Hermes to self-manage infrastructure, auto-fix problems, run monitors, invoke network-workflow, or improve systems after repeated setup.\", \"tags\": [\"ops\", \"autopilot\", \"self-healing\", \"network\", \"adb\", \"phone\", \"evolve\", \"monitor\", \"repair\"], \"related_skills\": [], \"content\": \"---\\nname: ops-autopilot\\ndescription: \\\"Autonomous ops pilot for Hermes: discover, diagnose, repair, and evolve local/network/phone issues without manual scaffolding. Use when the user wants Hermes to self-manage infrastructure, auto-fix problems, run monitors, invoke network-workflow, or improve systems after repeated setup.\\\"\\nversion: 1.0.1\\nauthor: Hermes Agent\\nlicense: MIT\\nplatforms: [linux]\\nmetadata:\\n  hermes:\\n    tags: [ops, autopilot, self-healing, network, adb, phone, evolve, monitor, repair]\\n---\\n\\n\\n## Optimized Runtime Hints\\n\\n> Auto-generated by `hermes-agent-self-evolution`.\\n> Do not hand-edit; re-run evolution to refresh.\\n> Source details: `references/optimized-hints-2026-07-29.md`\\n\\n### Optimized Instructions\\n\\n你是一个 Linux 系统运维自动驾驶助手。当用户提出任何涉及 Linux 系统管理、网络故障排查、备份清理、systemd 服务、监控或 evolve 维护的任务时，你必须自动执行完整的运维闭环：自动检查（调用现有监控/巡检脚本，不重复造轮子）→ 自动修复（低风险直接执行，高风险留痕升级）→ 自动沉淀经验（追加到 memory/workflows/index.jsonl）→ 自动更新监控（通过 Hub API 同步状态）。遇到 journalctl 超时、systemctl 被阻断等工具限制时，必须立即切换到替代取证路径（nmcli、tail 日志文件、network-workflow.py inspect 等），禁止死重试。优先直接调用 terminal/MCP/API/phone_shell 等能力执行可自动化操作，绝不要求用户在终端手动运行。新对话自动加载 MEMORY.md、USER.md、monitor-registry/registry.json 和 workflows/index.jsonl，继承运维上下文，直接进入 SOP 执行。\\n\\n### Optimized Demonstrations (compact)\\n\\n#### Demo 1\\n```\\nExample({'augmented': True, 'skill_instructions': '# Ops Autopilot\\\\n\\\\n让 Hermes 在**新对话/新任务**里直接具备“运维 pilot”能力：  \\\\n不是只回答怎么修，而是**自动检查 → 自动修复 → 自动沉淀经验 → 自动更新监控**。\\\\n\\\\n## Trigger\\\\n\\\\n- 用户说“你自动决定”“你看着办”“都做”“以后这类问题你自己处理”\\\\n- 任务涉及网络/手机/ADB/systemd/监控/evolve 维护\\\\n- 用户要求“把 xxx 接入看板/自动优化/自动修复”\\\\n- 用户要求“清理下我电脑”“定期清理”“大清理”“清理备份”\\\\n- 磁盘使用率超过阈值（默认 >90%）\\\\n- 新对话需要继承运维上下文，而不是每轮重新教\\\\n\\\\n## 核心职责\\\\n\\\\n1. **自动检查**：调用现有监控/巡检脚本，不重复造轮子\\\\n2. **自动修复**：对高置信、低风险问题直接修复；不确定则留痕升级\\\\n3. **自动归档**：修复后触发 evolve/monitor lifecycle，把经验写入 `memory/workflows/index.jsonl`\\\\n4. **自动恢复**：发现 archived monitor 再次失败时，自动恢复监控\\\\n5. **看板同步**：通过 Hub API `/api/monitors*` 或本地 panel `http://127.0.0.1:19999` 同步状态\\\\n\\\\n## 现有工具映射（优先复用，不新建）\\\\n\\\\n| 能力 | 路径/工具 | 调用方式 |\\\\n|------|----------|---------|\\\\n| 监控检查 | `~/.local/bin/monitor-check-and-lifecycle.py` | `terminal` 执行\\n```\\n\\n\\n\\n# Ops Autopilot\\n\\n让 Hermes 在**新对话/新任务**里直接具备“运维 pilot”能力：  \\n不是只回答怎么修，而是**自动检查 → 自动修复 → 自动沉淀经验 → 自动更新监控**。\\n\\n## Trigger\\n\\n- 用户说“你自动决定”“你看着办”“都做”“以后这类问题你自己处理”\\n- 任务涉及网络/手机/ADB/systemd/监控/evolve 维护\\n- 用户要求“把 xxx 接入看板/自动优化/自动修复”\\n- 用户要求“清理下我电脑”“定期清理”“大清理”“清理备份”\\n- 新对话需要继承运维上下文，而不是每轮重新教\\n\\n## 核心职责\\n\\n1. **自动检查**：调用现有监控/巡检脚本，不重复造轮子\\n2. **自动修复**：对高置信、低风险问题直接修复；不确定则留痕升级\\n3. **自动归档**：修复后触发 evolve/monitor lifecycle，把经验写入 `memory/workflows/index.jsonl`\\n4. **自动恢复**：发现 archived monitor 再次失败时，自动恢复监控\\n5. **看板同步**：通过 Hub API `/api/monitors*` 或本地 panel `http://127.0.0.1:19999` 同步状态\\n\\n## 现有工具映射（优先复用，不新建）\\n\\n| 能力 | 路径/工具 | 调用方式 |\\n|------|----------|---------|\\n| 监控检查 | `~/.local/bin/monitor-check-and-lifecycle.py` | `terminal` 执行 |\\n| 监控 CLI | `~/.local/bin/monitor-engine.py` | `terminal` 执行 |\\n| 网络巡检 | `~/.local/bin/network-workflow.py` | `terminal` 执行 |\\n| 系统清理 | `~/.local/bin/system-sanity-evolve` | `terminal` 执行 |\\n| 经验沉淀 | `~/.local/bin/hermes-evolve-now` | `terminal` 执行 |\\n| 看板 API | `http://127.0.0.1:9800/api/monitors` | `web` 或 `browser` |\\n| 看板面板 | `http://127.0.0.1:19999` | `browser` 打开 |\\n| 手机 MCP | `mcp_phone_connect_*` | 直接工具调用 |\\n| Hermes 日志 | `~/.hermes/logs/agent.log` | `read_file` / `terminal` |\\n\\n## 标准作业程序（SOP）\\n\\n### 0. 结果输出格式（用户强制要求）\\n- 运维巡检/修复任务默认返回结构化 JSON：\\n  ```json\\n  {\\\"status\\\":\\\"done|error\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"1-2句话\\\",\\\"artifacts\\\":[]}\\n  ```\\n- `summary` 只写结论和已修复项；`artifacts` 只放本次变更/产出的关键文件路径。\\n- 不要返回长 Markdown 报告；若需留痕，写入 `references/` 或脚本输出文件后，在 `artifacts` 中列路径。\\n\\n### 1. 发现阶段\\n\\n- 先读 `~/.hermes/memories/MEMORY.md` 和 `~/.hermes/memories/USER.md`，加载已有偏好\\n- 再读 `~/.local/state/monitor-registry/registry.json` 和 `history.jsonl`，了解已知问题\\n- 运行 `monitor-engine.py summary` 和 `network-workflow.py inspect` 收集现状\\n- **MCP 卫生检查**：`~/.hermes/config.yaml` 的 `mcp_servers:` 里启用项是否过多？工具 schema 会直接注入 system prompt，不是 memory 压缩能管住的。如果最近 7 天没用的 MCP，优先禁用\\n\\n### 2. 诊断阶段\\n\\n- 对 network/phone/service 问题，优先查：\\n  - `~/.hermes/logs/agent.log`\\n  - `~/.local/state/monitor-registry/history.jsonl`\\n  - `~/.local/state/network-workflow/latest.json`\\n  - `~/.local/state/system-sanity-evolve/latest.json`\\n- 不重复问用户已知信息；如果已有结论，直接进入修复\\n\\n### 3. 修复阶段\\n\\n- **低风险/高置信**：直接改配置、重启服务、清理状态、更新 monitor\\n- **中风险**：先备份，再修复，写 `auto-cleanup.log` 或 `history.jsonl`\\n- **高风险**：不执行，只给出方案和风险说明\\n- 修复后必须验证：\\n  - 服务是否 active\\n  - 端口是否 open\\n  - 手机是否可连\\n  - monitor 是否从 fail 转为 ok\\n\\n### 4. 沉淀阶段\\n\\n- 运行 `hermes-evolve-now` 或直接写 `~/.local/state/hermes-evolve/hermes-task-journal.jsonl`\\n- 把本次修复经验追加到 `memory/workflows/index.jsonl`\\n- 高置信规则同时写入 `~/.ai-context/runbooks/system-sanity-evolve.md`\\n\\n### 5. 看板同步\\n\\n- 确保 `hub-api.py` 的 `/api/monitors*` 可返回最新数据\\n- 如用户要求接入看板，直接打开 `http://127.0.0.1:19999` 或 `/static/monitor.html`\\n- 不修改 Hermes Web UI 打包文件；通过 Hub API 或独立 panel 接入\\n\\n## 自动决策规则\\n\\n- **用户说“你自动决定”**：默认执行，不列选项\\n- **遇到唯一可行路径**：直接执行，不解释过多\\n- **遇到多路径**：选最短闭环路径执行，不展开对比\\n- **不确定风险**：先只读检查，再决定是否修复\\n- **失败重试**：最多 3 次，状态写入 `/tmp/job-watchdog-state.json`\\n- **有工具/通道可直接执行时，绝不要求用户在终端手动运行**：MCP、terminal、API、phone_shell、ADB wrapper、curl 等现有能力可直接落地的操作，必须直接调用并返回结果；禁止把明明可由 agent 执行的步骤转嫁给用户在终端手动敲。用户历史上对这类行为有过明确纠正（“那你之前为啥不自己调用”），属于第一优先级风格约束。手机/网络/服务类任务尤其要直接执行，不要反问“你要我帮我改吗”或“你要我执行吗”。\\n\\n## 多问题并行回答规则\\n\\n- 当用户一次性提出多个问题时，必须逐条回答，不要只深入其中一条而忽略其他\\n- 优先回答最直接/最简单的问题（如“是否有开源项目”），再进入复杂调试\\n- 如果用户的问题包含“背景 + 具体故障”，先确认背景问题的答案，再处理故障\\n- 典型错误：用户问“A 存在吗？B 能装吗？C 为啥不显示？”，只回答 C 而完全忽略 A/B\\n\\n## FRP / 端口转发自动修复 SOP\\n\\n当用户反馈“公网打不开 Hermes/8787/5000/18300/18094”或 FRP 相关端口 timeout 时，按以下闭环执行，不要只诊断不修复。\\n\\n### 1. 取证顺序（最多 4 步，不要更多）\\n\\n0. DuckDNS 漂移检测：若公网域名访问 timeout，先执行 `phone-hermes-network/references/duckdns-drift-auto-fix.md` 中的检测流程，确认 WAN IP 与 DuckDNS 解析一致。\\n1. `journalctl --user -u frpc --since '2min ago'`：看 `start proxy success` 还是 `connect to local service ... i/o timeout`\\n2. `sudo ss -ltnp | grep ':18300|:18094|<port>'`：确认 `frps` 是否监听\\n3. `curl 127.0.0.1:<port>`：确认本地服务是否正常\\n4. 路由器 DNAT：`sshpass -p admin ssh ... admin@192.168.123.1 \\\"iptables -t nat -L vserver -n --line-numbers\\\" | grep '<port>'`，确认 remotePort 是否 DNAT 到 **Fedora LAN IP**\\n\\n### 2. 自动修复决策\\n\\n| 现象 | 自动修复动作 | 风险 |\\n|------|-------------|------|\\n| `frpc` 日志 `start error: port unavailable` | 检查 `/etc/frp/frps.toml` 的 `allowPorts`，若缺失则追加并重启 `frps` | 低 |\\n| 路由器 DNAT 目标不是 Fedora LAN IP | **不自动改路由器**，输出 exact `iptables` 规则让用户确认，或引导登录 Padavan 修改 | 中 |\\n| firewalld 未放行 | `sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-port=<port>/tcp && sudo firewall-cmd --reload` | 低 |\\n| `frps` 未监听 | `systemctl restart frps`，然后 `ss -ltnp | grep <port>` | 低 |\\n\\n### 3. 验证闭环\\n\\n修复后必须执行：\\n```bash\\n# 本机\\ncurl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\\\n' 127.0.0.1:<port>\\n\\n# 手机 5G（如可用）\\nadb -s 100.87.37.3:5555 shell \\\"curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}s\\\\n' --connect-timeout 5 http://<wan-ip>:<port>/\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### 4. 与导航面板联动\\n\\n如果用户有 5000 导航面板，修复完成后自动更新面板中的 `frp` 列 URL，确保 `TARGETS` 和 `renderPageAddrs()` 同步。\\n\\n### 5. FRP transport 调优（高延迟 / 5G 场景）\\n\\n随身 WiFi / 5G 下如果 `frpc` 日志频繁出现 `connect to local service ... i/o timeout` 或公网端口间歇性 502，先调 `transport.poolCount`：\\n\\n```toml\\n# /var/home/charlie/.config/frpc/frpc.toml\\ntransport.heartbeatInterval = 10\\ntransport.heartbeatTimeout = 120\\ntransport.poolCount = 20   # 默认 5，高延迟场景改 20\\n```\\n\\n改后重启并验证：\\n\\n```bash\\nsystemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user restart frpc\\nsystemctl --user status frpc --no-pager | head -n 15\\n```\\n\\n### 6. 本地 vs 公网端口测试方法论\\n\\nPython `requests` 会继承环境变量 `http_proxy`，因此对公网 IP 测试可能拿到本地代理的 502，误判为 FRP 故障。必须区分：\\n\\n```bash\\n# 走本地代理（可能 502）\\npython3 -c \\\"import requests; print(requests.get('http://103.121.208.125:18300/').status_code)\\\"\\n\\n# 直连公网（真实 FRP 可达性）\\ncurl -sv --noproxy '*' http://103.121.208.125:18300/ 2>&1 | head -n 20\\n```\\n\\n- 如果 `curl --noproxy '*'` 返回 `connection refused`，而本地 `curl 127.0.0.1:18300` 正常 → 问题在路由器 DNAT / 运营商入站过滤，不是 Hermes 或 frpc。\\n- 如果 `curl --noproxy '*'` 返回 `200` → 本地代理干扰，修本地代理配置即可。\\n\\n### 7. 本地 Node.js 代理脚本卫生\\n\\n当修改 `/var/home/charlie/.local/bin/hermes-8648-http-proxy.js` 等常驻代理脚本时：\\n- 调试完成后删除所有 `console.log / console.error`，避免 systemd journal 被代理噪音淹没。\\n- 确认 `Host` 头被强制写成后端真实地址（`127.0.0.1:18648`），不要把前端来的 `:8648` 原样转发。\\n\\n## 综合管理工具选型\\n\\n当用户问“有没有一个面板统一管 FRP/DDNS/端口/5G/NetBird”时，给出分级建议：\\n\\n1. **轻量智能体方案（推荐）**：继续用现有脚本 + ops-autopilot。优势是贴合现有环境、可直接执行自动修复、不引入新依赖。适合已经把大量逻辑固化成脚本的用户。\\n2. **`gdy666/lucky`**：8k+ stars 的 Go 语言软硬路由面板，覆盖 FRP、DDNS、端口转发、反向代理、cron、ACME、WebDAV/FTP。适合想用统一 Web UI 管理路由器/旁路由场景，**不刷固件**，用户态运行。缺点是它是通用工具，不理解 NetBird/5G 手机专项逻辑，需要额外做监控脚本对接。\\n3. **`netbirdio/dashboard`**：581 stars，仅 NetBird 官方管理 UI，不管 FRP/路由器端口。\\n4. **nezha-dashboard**：偏监控告警，不做转发配置。\\n\\n**结论**：没有开源项目天然覆盖“Padavan + NetBird + 5G + FRPS”四层并自带自动修复。最优解是“轻量脚本做专项 + 智能体做闭环 + 可选 lucky 做 FRP/DDNS 统一 UI”。\\n\\n## 本地 Web UI 的 WebSocket Multiplex 调试\\n\\n当调试类似 WsScrcpyWeb 的本地投屏/Web UI 服务时，注意：\\n\\n1. **先理解协议再改代码**：WsScrcpyWeb 使用 MULTIPLEX + 通道类型（HSTS/GTRC/FSLS/SHEL）区分设备列表、控制、流、文件等通道\\n2. **前端 class 必须和后端 channel handler 对齐**：\\n   - HostTracker → HSTS（设备列表）\\n   - GoogDeviceTracker → GTRC（设备通道/流）\\n   - RemoteShell → SHEL\\n   - FileListing → FSLS\\n3. **关键方法必须实现**：\\n   - `supportMultiplexing(){return!0}`\\n   - `getChannelCode(){return <TYPE>}`\\n   - `getChannelInitData(){return <init data>}`\\n4. **不要部分修改 processChannel**：后端 `processChannel` 通常接受多种通道类型，只保留一种会导致其他 Tracker 建连失败\\n5. **验证顺序**：改完代码后先看前端 Network/WS 帧，再看后端日志，确认通道建立成功\\n\\n## Answer-first 与反循环规则\\n\\n- **先给结论，再执行**：用户明确偏好“先给结论再执行”。只要已有足够证据形成初步结论，立即给出答案/状态摘要，不要把剩余时间浪费在重复验证上。\\n- **同类命令最多 2 次**：同一条 `grep`/`curl`/`ss` 命令连续返回相同结果时，第 3 次起视为死循环前兆，必须换思路或直接回答。\\n- **状态类问题用状态矩阵回答**：当用户问“hermes cli / studio / 8787 / openhands 是否都接入了某系统”，优先用 `systemctl --user status` + `config.yaml` + 脚本引用做一次 2x2 覆盖检查，输出“组件 vs 能力”矩阵，不要反复 grep。\\n- **不要用工具执行代替思考**：terminal/read_file/grep 是取证手段，不是答案本身。每 3-5 次工具调用后，若没有新信息，强制回退一步，写一句当前结论再决定下一步。\\n- **Device-auth / OAuth 必须自动开浏览器**：当 CLI 产出设备码授权链接时，必须先自动调用系统浏览器打开 URL；不要停留在“你可以打开这个链接”让用户手动。典型流程：先拿到 `code` + URL，再立即执行 `xdg-open <url>`（失败时回退为打印链接），最后只补一句最小提醒。\\n\\n## Phone / ADB 连接兜底规则\\n\\n- **不要把 phone MCP 的 `connected: false` 当成最终结论**。Phone MCP 受 NetBird/Tailscale/FRP/USB 多路由影响，某一路径失败不代表设备不可达。\\n- **必须按记忆中的已知地址/端口做兜底探测**，至少包括：\\n  - 局域网直连：`192.168.123.22:5555`\\n  - NetBird：`100.87.37.3:5555`\\n  - FRP/SSH：`100.87.37.3:8022`\\n  - USB reverse：`127.0.0.1:15555`\\n- 探测顺序：先 `adb kill-server && adb start-server`，再逐个 `adb connect`，最后 `adb devices -l` 确认。\\n- 用户若补充“我在局域网 / NetBird 关了”，要立即切换到剩余路径继续连，不要停在“不可达”。\\n\\n## Android IME 典型坑\\n\\n- **空白输入法 / 看起来“没弹界面”**：优先检查 `FlexImeService.onCreateInputView()` 是否在创建 `FlexKeyboardView` 后立即调用 `loadLayout(currentLayoutId)` 或 `keyboardView.render(...)`。没渲染时，输入法视图可能高度为 0 或空，用户会感觉“没有弹出”。\\n- **设置项存在但看不到**：先确认 `AndroidManifest.xml` 的 `<service ... android:permission=\\\"android.permission.BIND_INPUT_METHOD\\\">` 和 `<meta-data android:name=\\\"android.view.im\\\" android:resource=\\\"@xml/method\\\" />` 是否正常。\\n\\n## 本地脚本健康检查 SOP\\n\\n当用户要求“测试脚本是否正常”“验证路由脚本”“检查 xxx 能不能用”时，按三层验证执行，不直接复述错误就停。\\n\\n### 0. 结果输出格式（用户强制要求）\\n- 脚本验证任务默认返回结构化 JSON：\\n  ```json\\n  {\\\"status\\\":\\\"done|error\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"1-2句话\\\",\\\"artifacts\\\":[]}\\n  ```\\n- `summary` 只写结论和关键证据；`artifacts` 只放本次验证涉及的关键脚本/日志路径。\\n- 不要返回长 Markdown 报告；若需留痕，写入 `references/` 后在 `artifacts` 中列路径。\\n\\n### 1. 语法 / 静态检查\\n- Python：`python3 -m py_compile <script>`\\n- Bash：`bash -n <script>`\\n- Node/TS：先看 `tsc --noEmit` 或 `node --check`，视项目约定\\n\\n### 2. 逻辑 / 单测（无外部依赖）\\n- 对核心函数做离线单测：直接 `python3 -c` 或 `node -e` 注入测试用例\\n- 重点测：路由/分发/分类函数、配置解析、边界输入\\n- **注意**：模块名含连字符时不能 `import xxx-yyy`，必须用 `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location`\\n\\n### 3. 外部依赖探针\\n- API 类依赖用最小 payload 探活：`curl -s -o /dev/null -w \\\"%{http_code}\\\" ...`\\n- 区分“脚本故障”与“外部限流/不可达”：429/5xx 通常是外部状态，不说明脚本本身坏了\\n- 记录最终结论矩阵：语法 ✅/❌、逻辑 ✅/❌、外部依赖 ✅/❌\\n\\n### 4. 路由脚本专项验证\\n- 当用户要求“测试路由脚本”且目标同时包含 systemd 服务与路由函数时，分两层验证：\\n  1. 服务探活：`systemctl --user status <service>` + `timeout 5 bash -c 'echo > /dev/tcp/127.0.0.1/<port>'`\\n  2. 核心逻辑：用 `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` 直接 import 脚本中的路由/分类函数并注入测试用例\\n- 若外部依赖（如 `/api/chat-run/runs`）已知不稳定，不要重复跑端到端测试；只验证本地逻辑和本地服务可达即可\\n\\n## 与 Hermes 新对话的兼容方式\\n\\n新对话不需要用户重新交代背景，Hermes 应主动：\\n\\n1. 读取 `MEMORY.md` / `USER.md` 加载偏好\\n2. 读取 `monitor-registry/registry.json` 加载已知问题\\n3. 读取 `workflows/index.jsonl` 加载历史经验\\n4. 遇到运维问题时，直接进入 SOP\\n\\n### 默认自动加载\\n\\nThis skill is treated as an auto-loaded default skill. New conversations inherit it through `~/.hermes/SOUL.md`, which instructs Hermes to invoke `ops-autopilot` whenever the task involves local/network/phone/ADB/systemd/monitoring/evolve ops. If the current session does not already have this context, assume it and proceed without re-asking for setup paths.\\n\\n## Home 目录 AI 记忆感知清理\\n\\n当用户要求“大清理”“定期清理”或涉及 `/home`、`备份`、`codex`、`opencode`、`.hermes` 时，必须先识别并保留 AI 记忆/状态文件，再执行清理。\\n\\n### 必须保留的 AI 记忆/状态文件\\n\\n| 路径 | 类型 | 说明 |\\n|------|------|------|\\n| `~/.hermes/memories/` | 长期记忆 | Hermes MEMORY.md / USER.md / 归档记忆 |\\n| `~/.hermes/state.db` | 状态数据库 | 对话/任务状态，不要删除 |\\n| `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db` | 上下文历史 | OpenCode 对话数据库 |\\n| `~/.local/state/codex-account-manager/` | 账号配置 | Codex 回退账号/fallback 配置 |\\n| `~/.openhands/` | 状态 | OpenHands 会话状态 |\\n| `~/.codex-10-login/` | 登录态 | 当前活跃 Codex 登录信息 |\\n| `~/.sdkman/` | 工具链 | SDKMAN Java/Gradle 工具链，按需保留 |\\n| `~/.gradle/` | 构建缓存 | Gradle 缓存，可清理旧版本 transform/instrumented jar |\\n\\n### 可安全清理的会话/日志文件\\n\\n| 路径 | 说明 |\\n|------|------|\\n| `~/.codex*/logs_2.sqlite` | 各 slot 的会话日志，不是长期记忆；可清旧 slot，保留最新 1-2 个 |\\n| `~/.codex.bak.*/logs_2.sqlite` | 旧备份登录态，已迁移则删除 |\\n| `~/.local/state/codex-account-manager/timer.log` | 轮转日志，按大小/时间清理 |\\n\\n### 备份目录清理策略\\n\\n1. **优先保留最新一次完整备份**，如 `backup_20260726_*`\\n2. **如已有同名 `.tar.gz`，可删除解压目录**，如 `backup_20260724_224130/` 保留 `backup_20260724_224130.tar.gz`\\n3. **删除 30 天以上的旧备份目录**，如 `20260626_*`\\n4. **清理前统计文件数和总大小**：\\n   ```bash\\n   find 备份 -type f | wc -l\\n   find 备份 -type f -printf '%s\\\\n' | awk '{s+=$1} END{print s}'\\n   ```\\n\\n### Waydroid 镜像清理\\n\\n- 先确认 session 状态：`waydroid status`\\n- 如 Session 为 `STOPPED`，可删除 `/var/lib/waydroid/images/system.img` 和 `vendor.img`（共约 2.3G）\\n- 不要碰 `/var/lib/waydroid/data/`，那是用户数据\\n\\n### Sub2API 旧二进制清理\\n\\n- 先确认运行版本：`/var/opt/sub2api/sub2api --version`\\n- 如存在 `.bak-<version>` 且运行版本更新，可删除旧备份\\n- 示例：运行 0.1.162 时，可删 `sub2api.bak-0.1.149`\\n\\n### 定期清理 cron 建议\\n\\n清理完成后，为用户生成或更新 `crontab -e`：\\n\\n```cron\\n# 每天凌晨 3 点清理过期容器和 dangling images\\n0 3 * * * /usr/bin/podman container prune -f && /usr/bin/podman image prune -f\\n# 每周日清理 journal 到 200M\\n0 4 * * 0 root /usr/bin/journalctl --vacuum-size=200M\\n# 每周日清理 /var/tmp 7 天前的文件\\n0 4 * * 0 /usr/bin/find /var/tmp -type f -atime +7 -delete\\n```\\n\\n## MCP 上下文治理\\n\\n### 为什么 MCP 会塞满上下文\\n\\n- **Memory 是精简的**：`MEMORY.md` / `USER.md` 会按 `memory_char_limit` 裁剪\\n- **MCP 工具不是记忆**：每个工具的 `name + description + inputSchema` 都要完整注入 system prompt，作为 function calling 契约\\n- **工具越多，schema 越重**：`phone-connect`、`hermes-studio-api`、`firecrawl` 等每个都暴露大量工具，直接抢占上下文预算\\n\\n### 治理规则\\n\\n1. **先找现成方案，不要一上来就禁用。** 优先检查是否已有 proxy、router、hub integration 或工具合并方案可以在不丢能力的前提下减少 schema 注入。禁用 MCP 是最后手段，不是首选。\\n2. **最小必要原则**：如果确实需要精简，只保留当前场景必需 3-5 个 MCP server；其余设成 `enabled: false`\\n3. **按 profile 拆分**：不同任务用不同 Hermes profile，每个 profile 只启用相关 MCP\\n4. **禁用而不是卸载**：保留配置，只是 `enabled: false`，需要时可快速恢复\\n5. **验证影响**：禁用后重启 `hermes-web-ui.service`，确认新对话上下文占用下降\\n\\n### 快速审计命令\\n\\n```bash\\n# 查看当前启用的 MCP server 数量\\ngrep -c \\\"enabled: true\\\" ~/.hermes/config.yaml\\n\\n# 查看哪些 server 暴露工具最多\\ngrep -A2 \\\"enabled: true\\\" ~/.hermes/config.yaml | grep -E \\\"^\\\\\\\\s+[a-z]\\\" | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20\\n```\\n\\n### 典型可安全禁用的 MCP\\n\\n| MCP | 建议 | 理由 |\\n|-----|------|------|\\n| `firecrawl` | 按需启用 | 爬取/搜索专用，日常对话不必须 |\\n| `codex-account-manager` | 按需启用 | Sub2API 账号管理专用 |\\n| `haven` | 按需启用 | 手机定位/状态专用 |\\n| `mobile-browser-bridge` | 按需启用 | 手机浏览器 UI 专用 |\\n| `khoj` | 按需启用 | 个人知识库检索专用 |\\n| `playwright` | 已禁用 | 浏览器自动化，当前 headless 模式不必须 |\\n| `vision` | 已禁用 | 视觉分析专用 |\\n| `tablet` | 已禁用 | 平板专用 |\\n\\n## Phone MCP bridge and network quirks\\n\\nSee `references/phone-network-mcp-bridge.md` for:\\n- mihomo fake-ip GitHub fix\\n- ADB forward port-selection pattern when host port 8080 is occupied\\n- Stable phone connection recovery after `Connection reset by peer`\\n\\n## Linux 内存与 AI 服务资源整合\\n\\n当用户反馈“电脑很卡”“内存不够”“swap 满了”且环境中有大量 AI 服务（letta、opencode、hermes、litellm、matrix-wechat、podman 容器等）时，按以下顺序执行，不要上来就加 swap 或重启机器。\\n\\n### 执行顺序\\n1. **先磁盘，后内存**：根分区或 `/tmp` 100% 会阻塞 swap 写入和临时文件，先清理 `/tmp`、`/var/tmp`、journal 归档\\n2. **收紧 systemd-oomd**：检查是否已有 oomd，通过 dropin 收紧阈值（建议 `DefaultMemoryPressureLimit=50%`、`DefaultMemoryPressureDurationSec=15s`、`SwapUsedLimit=80%`）\\n3. **服务级内存边界**：为关键服务设置 `MemoryHigh/MemoryMax/SwapMax`\\n4. **容器级内存边界**：对 podman 容器用 `podman update --memory/--memory-swap` 限制\\n5. **验证脚本**：写入 `~/.local/bin/memory-check.sh` 作为现场保留和复检工具\\n\\n### 关键坑：podman 生成的 systemd service\\n- `podman-system-generator` 会把容器生成到 `/run/systemd/generator/`，这是临时目录，重启会丢\\n- 要给这些服务加 dropin，必须写到 `/etc/systemd/system/<service>.d/` 下\\n- 常见受影响的 AI 服务：`sub2api-postgres`、`sub2api-redis`、`letta-db` 等\\n- 如果 dropin 目录不存在，先 `mkdir -p`，否则 `tee` 会报错“没有那个文件或目录”\\n\\n### 容器限制持久化\\n- `podman update --memory` 只对运行中容器生效，重启后丢失\\n- 要持久化，必须回填到对应的 quadlet（`/etc/containers/systemd/*.container`）或 compose 文件\\n- 在 quadlet 里加 `Memory=2g`、`MemorySwap=3g`、`MemoryHigh=256m` 等参数\\n\\n### 快速审计命令\\n```bash\\nfree -h && swapon --show\\nsystemd-analyze cat-config systemd/oomd.conf\\nsystemctl show <service> -p MemoryCurrent,MemoryHigh,MemoryMax,SwapPeak\\npodman inspect --format '{{.Name}}\\\\\\\\t{{.HostConfig.Memory}}\\\\\\\\t{{.HostConfig.MemorySwap}}' $(podman ps -a -q)\\n```\\n\\n### 验证清单\\n- `free -h` 和 `swapon --show` 确认内存/Swap 余量\\n- `systemd-analyze cat-config systemd/oomd.conf` 确认 oomd 配置加载\\n- `systemctl show <service> -p MemoryCurrent,MemoryHigh,MemoryMax` 确认限制生效\\n- `podman inspect --format '{{.Name}}\\\\\\\\t{{.HostConfig.Memory}}\\\\\\\\t{{.HostConfig.MemorySwap}}'` 确认容器限制\\n\\n## 本地服务导航 / 连通性看板\\n\\n当用户要求“把 8787/8648 的地址做成网页导航”“做一个能检测手机能否访问的导航页”“5000面板互相跳转兜底”时，直接复用 `templates/nav-server.py` + `templates/nav-index.html` 部署独立 Python HTTP 服务，不要试图往现有 Hermes 代理（如 8648）挂载静态文件。\\n\\n部署要点：\\n1. 创建项目目录（如 `~/workspace/nav/`），放入模板文件\\n2. 修改 `TARGETS` 数组中的服务名称和地址\\n3. `chmod +x server.py` 并创建 systemd user unit（`Type=simple`, `Restart=on-failure`）\\n4. 防火墙开放对应端口：`sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-port=<port>/tcp && sudo firewall-cmd --reload`\\n5. 手机验证：`adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d \\\"http://<ip>:<port>/\\\"`\\n6. 如 DuckDNS 解析 IP 与当前 WAN 不一致，顶部会自动显示漂移警告\\n\\n### 实时缓存与预加载模式（2026-07-30 新增）\\n\\n用户明确要求“一点击就用，不要等”。实现要点：\\n- 后端用后台线程每 2-3 秒批量探测所有路径，结果写入 `_cache`\\n- 前端 `/api/status`、`/api/ntfy`、`/api/jump` 直接返回缓存，不实时探测\\n- 用双锁分离状态缓存和通知缓存：`_status_lock` / `_ntfy_lock`，避免相互阻塞\\n- ntfy 等长连接/慢响应接口用 `requests.get(..., stream=True)` 分块读取，避免 `urllib` 阻塞整个服务\\n\\n### 跨路径兜底跳转（2026-07-30 新增）\\n\\n用户要求 NetBird/Tailscale/LAN/FRP 互相跳转。实现要点：\\n- 新增 `/api/jump?service=<服务名>`：对指定服务只返回当前 `reachable=True` 的路径\\n- 前端每个卡片显示“快速访问”按钮，调用 `/api/fastest` 自动打开延迟最低的可用路径\\n- 前端显示“本页访问地址”列表，方便手动切换\\n\\n### ntfy 通知整合（2026-07-30 新增）\\n\\n用户要求整合 ntfy 并过滤无效消息。实现要点：\\n- 用 `since=1h` 拉取历史消息，避免 `poll=0` 长轮询阻塞\\n- 过滤纯 `open` 事件（无实际内容）\\n- 只保留最近 12 条有效消息，按时间倒序\\n- 支持 `charlie-actions`、`charlie-network`、`phone-run` 等多个 topic\\n\\n### 5G 公网不可达的永久处理（2026-07-30 新增）\\n\\n用户反馈“100.87.31.44:5000 打不开”“125.110.209.185:8787 打不开”，要求永久解决。\\n- 根因：手机 5G 到路由器 WAN IP（125.110.209.185）全端口超时，是运营商 CG-NAT/路由策略，不是本地配置问题\\n- 不要在 5000 面板里对 5G 公网路径做高频重试；把 NetBird/Tailscale/LAN 作为主力，FRP 公网作为可选\\n- 路由器 DNAT 修正后，只在本机/WLAN 下验证 FRP 公网路径；手机 5G 验证超时时应直接判定为“公网不可达”，提示用户走内网穿透\\n\\n详细模式说明见 `references/local-connectivity-dashboard.md`。\\n\\n## Hermes MCP 路由脚本诊断（`mcp-smart-router` / `hermes-workflow-router`）\\n见 `references/hermes-mcp-router-auth.md`。核心结论：\\n- `list_profiles` / `auto_profile` / `hermes-workflow-router` 可正常返回时，只说明本地路由逻辑有效。\\n- 若 `route_task_mcp` 返回 `HTTP 401`，优先查 Hermes Web UI token / session token / API base 鉴权，不要重复重启服务。\\n- 验证顺序：profile 查询 → 自动推荐 → 只读路由接口 → 鉴权失败时单独排查 token/env。\\n\\n## 相关文件\\n\\n- `~/.local/bin/monitor-check-and-lifecycle.py`\\n- `~/.local/bin/network-workflow.py`\\n- `~/.local/bin/system-sanity-evolve`\\n- `~/.local/bin/hermes-evolve-now`\\n- `~/.config/monitors/monitors.yaml`\\n- `~/.local/state/monitor-registry/`\\n- `~/.hermes/memories/MEMORY.md`\\n- `hub/hub-api.py` 中的 `/api/monitors*` 路由\\n- `templates/nav-server.py` — 本地连通性导航后端模板\\n- `templates/nav-index.html` — 本地连通性导航前端模板\\n- `references/local-connectivity-dashboard.md` — 双视角探测模式、hairpin 绕行、DuckDNS 漂移检测\\n- `references/frp-auto-repair.md` — FRP/端口转发自动修复 SOP（已内嵌于 SKILL.md）\\n- `phone-hermes-network/references/lucky-vs-lightweight.md` — lucky 与轻量脚本选型对比\\n- `references/adb-auth-fix.md` — ADB RSA popup root cause, disconnect blocking, Magisk key watchdog, and verification steps\\n- `references/mcp-context-hygiene.md` — Why MCP schemas consume context, audit commands, safe disable list, and profile-based MCP segmentation\\n- `references/hermes-cli-tmux-duckdns-access.md` — Local tmux entry, Haven wrapper pattern, `hermes --worktree` session isolation, and DuckDNS remote access topology for Hermes CLI\\n- `references/linux-memory-ai-tuning.md` — Linux memory optimization for AI services with systemd-oomd, podman memory limits, and verification scripts\\n- `references/skill-evolution-pipeline-fixes-2026-07-29.md` — Evolution pipeline bug fixes and eval quirks (baseline validation, DSPy API, LiteLLM base URL, holdout timeout mitigation, metrics-before-merge rule)\\n- `references/ws-scrcpyweb-multiplex-debugging.md` — WsScrcpyWeb WebSocket multiplex protocol, channel types (HSTS/GTRC/SHEL/FSLS), frontend/backend class mapping, and recovery patch order\\n- `references/podman-inspection-quirks.md` — podman 模板字段/资源采样/事件流/线程统计陷阱，以及 Docker/Podman 兼容与端口冲突速查\\n- `references/container-troubleshooting-playbook.md` — podman/docker emulation exit 125、host-network orphan takeover、shared PostgreSQL bootstrap、service reachability probes, appsmith/litellm/khoj stack fixes\\n- `references/hermes-8787-8648-streaming-proxy-playbook.md` — 8648 proxy Host-header fix、8787 zombie vs long-running task distinction、stream status API quick check、Python `requests` SSE limitation、FRP poolCount tuning、local vs public port testing methodology\\n\", \"path\": \"devops/ops-autopilot/SKILL.md\", \"skill_dir\": \"/var/home/charlie/.hermes/skills/devops/ops-autopilot\", \"linked_files\": {\"references\": [\"references/adb-auth-fix.md\", \"references/mcp-context-hygiene.md\", \"references/phone-network-mcp-bridge.md\", \"references/hermes-cli-tmux-duckdns-access.md\", \"references/linux-memory-ai-tuning.md\", \"references/mobile-blank-page-verification.md\", \"references/network-shutdown-investigation.md\", \"references/netbird-diagnosis.md\", \"references/netbird-tunnel-diagnostics.md\", \"references/phone-mcp-mount-dependency.md\", \"references/systemd-audit-pattern.md\", \"references/config-lock-unlock.md\", \"references/hermes-task-slowdown-playbook.md\", \"references/idle-scheduler-pattern.md\", \"references/systemd-restart-loop-playbook.md\", \"references/optimized-hints-2026-07-29.md\", \"references/skill-evolution-pipeline-fixes-2026-07-29.md\", \"references/ws-scrcpyweb-multiplex-debugging.md\", \"references/duckdns-public-port-diagnosis.md\", \"references/local-connectivity-dashboard.md\", \"references/podman-inspection-quirks.md\", \"references/container-troubleshooting-playbook.md\", \"references/hermes-8787-8648-streaming-proxy-playbook.md\", \"references/hermes-port-registry.md\"], \"templates\": [\"templates/nav-server.py\"], \"scripts\": [\"scripts/print-audit-summary.py\", \"scripts/wan-ip-monitor.sh\"]}, \"usage_hint\": \"To view linked files, call skill_view(name, file_path) where file_path is e.g. 'references/api.md' or 'assets/config.yaml'\", \"required_environment_variables\": [], \"required_commands\": [], \"missing_required_environment_variables\": [], \"missing_credential_files\": [], \"missing_required_commands\": [], \"setup_needed\": false, \"setup_skipped\": false, \"readiness_status\": \"available\", \"metadata\": {\"hermes\": {\"tags\": [\"ops\", \"autopilot\", \"self-healing\", \"network\", \"adb\", \"phone\", \"evolve\", \"monitor\", \"repair\"]}}}",
