/var/home/charlie/.hermes/skills/.archive/hermes-studio-task-automation/SKILL.md:44:3. **Write classification script**: Use `scripts/auto_triage.py` as the canonical template. The script reads **both** `~/.hermes/state.db` (CLI) and `~/.hermes-web-ui/hermes-web-ui.db` (Web UI), extracts user messages, classifies by keyword rules, and calls `hermes kanban create` with `HERMES_KANBAN_BOARD=<slug>` and `--idempotency-key <session_id>` to prevent duplicates. Important implementation notes: (a) build the classify text as a flat list of strings before joining, because mixing a list return value with string concatenation raises `TypeError`; (b) preload all existing `idempotency_key` values from every `~/.hermes/kanban/boards/*/kanban.db` **excluding archived tasks** before scanning new sessions, so re-runs stay idempotent; (c) for first rollout, route `high` confidence tasks into `active`, `medium` confidence into `pending-review`, and skip `low` confidence/non-task items entirely; (d) prefer a single `active` board in phase 1, and only fan out to `dev/ops/research/writing/design` boards after observing stable classification for 3-7 days.
